 "parsed": {
  "reachable": false,
  "rationale": "With mfa_admin and mfa_dbadmin deployed, every exfiltration route is blocked. The attacker can still get a long way in. exploit_web gives foothold_web. pivot_internal gives reach_internal, since segmented is false. steal_user_cred gives stolen_user. auth_ciserver works because mfa_user is false, and escalate_ciserver works because the CI server is unpatched, giving admin_ciserver. leak_secrets_ciserver then gives stolen_dbadmin. kerberoast gives stolen_admin. However, auth_dc and auth_adfs both require NOT mfa_admin, so they are blocked. Those are the only ways to get foothold_dc or foothold_adfs, so admin_dc and admin_adfs are unreachable. auth_db, auth_fileserver and auth_backup each require (NOT mfa_dbadmin OR admin_dc OR admin_adfs). That condition is false, so even with stolen_dbadmin no foothold on db, fileserver or backup can be obtained. As a result no admin_db, admin_fileserver or admin_backup is reachable, and exfiltrated stays false."
 },
